gs that are perhaps a little  different one is international  cooperation and the other is competition  i think different countries different  agencies different public and private  actors  are aiming to have their own capability  to access and operate at different  places in space and on the moon  as we build these different capabilities  we create competition it also drives  innovation it drives down costs and it  makes the space more accessible to  everybody so i think this is a very  positive thing  bringing together the value added of  working as a community in europe has  allowed us to achieve much more than any  country in europe could have achieved on  its own it's not just the sum of the  parts it's much greater than that  you

